# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# mITyGarden — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to apps/web/.env.local and fill in the values.
# VITE_ prefixed variables are embedded in the browser bundle at build time.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Google Maps API key (optional).
# If set, the wizard location step uses the Google Maps Geocoding API.
# If NOT set, the free OpenStreetMap Nominatim API is used automatically.
#
# Obtain a key at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# Enable the "Geocoding API" and "Maps Static API" for your project.
# Restrict the key to HTTP referrers (your domain) in the Cloud Console.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# ─── AI / LLM API keys ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# AI keys can be provided in two ways (environment variables take priority):
#
#   1. Via environment variables below (VITE_ prefix embeds them at build time).
#      Use this for server / container / CI deployments.
#
#   2. Via the in-app ⚙ Configure API Keys dialog (stored in browser localStorage).
#      Use this for individual user setups — no rebuild required.
#
# If a key is set both ways, the environment variable always wins.
#
# Obtain keys at:
#   OpenAI    → https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
#   Anthropic → https://console.anthropic.com
#   Gemini    → https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=
